# Administrators: members of the `sudo` group (devel on dev/desktop images;
# no account is in it on prod). Anything they run through sudo starts in
# sysadm_r:sysadm_t, the SELinux administrator domain, instead of inheriting
# the login domain (staff_t/user_t), which may not manage the system.
#
# The Defaults line also covers grants written elsewhere without ROLE/TYPE
# (for example a per-user NOPASSWD rule), because sudoers applies the last
# matching rule but Defaults per group apply to every rule.
#
# Needs: sudo built with SELinux support, and the account's SELinux user
# authorised for sysadm_r (seusers maps it to staff_u). A user mapped to
# user_u cannot hold sysadm_r, and sudo then refuses every command.
Defaults:%sudo role=sysadm_r, type=sysadm_t
%sudo ALL=(ALL:ALL) ROLE=sysadm_r TYPE=sysadm_t ALL
